## 8. Directory layout (required)

```
dupbuster/
├── android/.../scanengine/     # ScanEngine native (Android)
├── ios/ScanEngine/             # ScanEngine native (iOS)
├── src/
│   ├── components/             # UI catalog
│   ├── controllers/            # ScanSessionController
│   ├── tokens/tokens.ts
│   ├── screens/
│   └── types/
├── tests/fixtures/dupbuster/v1/  # Hash + security fixture matrix
└── .github/workflows/
```

New code must land in these areas unless architecture is amended first.

### 8.1 Scaffold (M1-01)

- **RN version:** 0.85.3 bare workflow; `applicationId` / bundle `com.dupbuster`.
- **Min OS:** `android/build.gradle` `minSdkVersion = 26`; iOS deployment **15.1** (Xcode project).
- **Install/run:** `npm install` → `npm start`; `npm run android` / `npm run ios` (iOS needs `cd ios && bundle exec pod install` on macOS).
- **Node:** `package.json` requires Node ≥ 22.11; use `nvm` if local Node is older.
- **Sign-off:** `./build.sh` not yet present — use `npm run lint` and `npm test` until M4 adds unified build script.
- **WSL Android builds:** Gradle/CMake in WSL require a **Linux** Android SDK (`sdk.dir` like `/home/<you>/Android/Sdk`) with NDK prebuilt `toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64`. A Windows SDK mounted at `/mnt/c/...` only has `windows-x86_64` — native modules (RN New Architecture) fail with missing `clang`. **Do not** symlink `windows-x86_64` as `linux-x86_64`. Use Windows SDK only when building from **Windows** (PowerShell), with `sdk.dir=C\:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Local\\Android\\Sdk`. Template: `android/local.properties.example`.
- **WSL emulator + build:** Linux SDK at `~/Android/Sdk` for Gradle/NDK (`sdk.dir` in `local.properties`). Run `bash scripts/setup-wsl-adb.sh` to install ELF `scripts/adb-proxy` as `platform-tools/adb` (forwards to Windows `adb.exe`; CRLF-safe `devices` output). Use `npm run android` → `scripts/run-android-wsl.sh` (`assembleDebug` + `adb install`) because Gradle `installDebug` uses DDMLib on WSL port 5037 and cannot see the Windows emulator. Fallback: `npm run android:rn` (stock RN; needs DDMLib bridge fix). Do not use shell `alias adb` for Gradle.
- **NDK version:** set via `ndkVersion` in `android/build.gradle` + `android/app/build.gradle`; do **not** use `ndk.dir` in `local.properties` (deprecated CXX5106).

### 8.2 ScanEngine Turbo Module interface (M1-02)

- **Turbo Module name:** `NativeScanEngine` — import runtime from `src/native/NativeScanEngine.ts`; use `src/types/scanEngine.ts` or `scanEngineBridge.types.ts` in Jest (no `TurboModuleRegistry` side effects).
- **Codegen:** `package.json` → `codegenConfig.name` = `ScanEngineSpec`, `jsSrcsDir` = `src/native`, `android.javaPackageName` = `com.dupbuster.scanengine`, iOS `modulesProvider.NativeScanEngine` → `RCTNativeScanEngine`.
- **Codegen constraint:** Bridge types for the spec must live **inline** in `NativeScanEngine.ts` (codegen does not follow imports from sibling files). Keep `scanEngineBridge.types.ts` aligned manually for Jest/controllers.
- **Android registration:** `ScanEnginePackage` in `MainApplication` `PackageList` (not autolinked).
- **Bridge surface:** Commands `startScan` / `pauseScan` / `resumeScan` / `cancelScan` / `deleteDuplicates` / `getCatalogMeta`; events `onScanProgress` / `onScanError` per `docs/architecture.md` §6.5 and §11.

### 8.3 UriValidator (M1-03)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.security.UriValidator` — call before every stat/open/hash; pure rules in `SafUriRules` (unit-tested).
- **iOS:** `DBUriValidator` — validates PHAsset `localIdentifier` (platform-fetch format) and security-scoped `file://` URLs; fail-closed → `PERMISSION_DENIED`.
- **Provenance:** `UriProvenance.USER_SUPPLIED` / `DBUriProvenanceUserSupplied` always denied (no pasted URIs).
- **SAF:** Reject `..` in document IDs (AC-security-uri-01); grant boundary via `DocumentsContract` tree/document IDs — no string path concatenation.
- **Tests:** `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest`; iOS `DupbusterScanEngineTests` target in Xcode.

### 8.4 DiscoveryEmitter mode A (M1-04)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.discovery.DiscoveryEmitter` — BFS over SAF tree via `DocumentsContract.buildChildDocumentsUriUsingTree` / `buildDocumentUriUsingTree`; inject `SafChildDocumentsQuery` in tests.
- **iOS:** `DBDiscoveryEmitter` — recursive `NSFileManager` enumeration under security-scoped DocumentPicker folder URLs (`file://`); `DBScanRootModeUserSelected` only.
- **Output:** `DiscoveredEntry` / `DBDiscoveredEntry` with `mediaTypeHint` wire values (`image`, `video`, `audio`, `document`, `text`, `other`); never bridge URIs/paths.
- **Validation:** Every candidate URI validated with `UriValidator` / `DBUriValidator` + `DISCOVERY` provenance before emit; denied counted, not emitted.
- **Batching:** `BATCH_SIZE` / 32 emitted files then yield; support `isCancelled` for pipeline cancel (M1-12).
- **Mode B** (MediaStore / PHAsset) is M1-05 — do not implement platform discovery union in M1-04.

### 8.5 DiscoveryEmitter mode B (M1-05)

- **Android:** `DiscoveryEmitter.emitModeB` — `MediaStoreDiscoveryQuery` over images, video, audio, downloads (downloads API 29+); dedupe by URI; `PlatformDiscoveryGrant` marker; optional `additionalSafGrants` (Mode A SAF union).
- **iOS:** `DBDiscoveryEmitter.emitModeBWithScanRootGrant:` — `DBPhAssetDiscoverySource` (default `DBPhotosPhAssetDiscoverySource`); limited library via `authorizedLocalIdentifiers`; optional scoped folder union with paired `additionalScopedFolderURLs` + `additionalScopedGrants`.
- **Output:** Mode B PHAsset → `phAssetLocalIdentifier` on `DBDiscoveredEntry`; MediaStore → `contentUri` on `DiscoveredEntry`. Never bridge identifiers.
- **Validation:** `UriValidator` / `DBUriValidator` with `PLATFORM_DISCOVERY` / `DBScanRootModePlatformDiscovery` + `DISCOVERY` provenance.
- **Tests:** inject `MediaStoreDiscoveryQuery` (Android); inject `DBPhAssetDiscoverySource` (iOS). Fixture `discovery-platform-discovery-01.json`.

### 8.6 StatStage (M1-06)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.stat.StatStage` — `UriValidator` gate then `ContentResolverFileStatReader` (`openFileDescriptor` + `Os.fstat`); inject `FileStatReader` in tests.
- **iOS:** `DBStatStage` — validates `file://` or PHAsset localIdentifier, then `DBFileStatReader` (`lstat` for scoped paths; PHAsset mtime only, null inode/device).
- **Output:** `StagedFile` / `DBStagedFile` with fresh size/mtime/inode/device_id/is_symlink + discovery metadata. Never bridge stat fields.
- **Symlinks:** iOS uses `lstat` only; Android best-effort via proc fd readlink. Full symlink fixture matrix is M1-17.
- **Video metadata** (duration_ms, width, height): M1-13+, not M1-06.
- **Tests:** inject `FileStatReader` (Android) / `DBFileStatReading` (iOS). Fixture `stat-content-uri-01.json`.

### 8.7 HashPipeline (M1-07)

- **Android:** `com.dupbuster.scanengine.hash.HashPipeline` — `InMemorySizeBucketIndex`, `Sha256Hasher`, inject `FileContentReader` in tests.
- **iOS:** `DBHashPipeline` + `DBSha256Hasher` (CommonCrypto); inject `DBFileContentReading` in tests.
- **Profiles in scope:** `RAW_BYTES`, `EMPTY:0` only — `TEXT_NFC_LF` is M1-08; `VIDEO_CONTENT_V1` is M1-13+.
- **Size bucket:** unique non-video sizes skip byte reads; video and zero-byte always hash; second file with same size triggers `NEEDS_HASH` (backfill prior skip is IndexWriter/orchestrator concern).
- **Caps:** 2 GB default skip (`LARGE_SKIPPED`) unless `HashSettings.largeFilesOptIn`; 120 s hash timeout → `HASH_TIMEOUT`.
- **Quick sample:** files > 50 MB store `quickSampleHash` (SHA-256 of first+last 64 KiB).
- **Symlinks:** `HashResult.SymlinkNode` / `DBHashPipelineOutcomeSymlinkNode` — no content read.
- **Tests:** inject content readers; fixture `hash-raw-bytes-01.json`.

